  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "The average age of \\(33\\) fifth-graders is \\(11.\\) The average age of \\(55\\) of their parents is \\(33.\\) What is the average age of all of these parents and fifth-graders?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( 22 \\)",
    "B": "\\( 23.25 \\)",
    "C": "\\( 24.75 \\)",
    "D": "\\( 26.25 \\)",
    "E": "\\( 28 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The groups have different sizes, so first recover each group's total age. The fifth-graders' total is \\(33\\cdot11=363\\) years, and the parents' total is \\(55\\cdot33=1815\\) years.\n\nThere are \\(33+55=88\\) people altogether. Their average age is therefore\n\\[\n\\frac{363+1815}{88}\n=\\frac{2178}{88}\n=\\boxed{24.75\\text{ years}}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\text{C}\\).",
